{
  "$schema": "https://developer.microsoft.com/json-schemas/fabric/item/dataAgent/definition/dataSource/1.0.0/schema.json",
  "artifactId": "210c14b4-028c-4db9-91f2-e617cd21a2dc",
  "workspaceId": "10327698-2b0d-446f-9b1b-beabe18a4bda",
  "dataSourceInstructions": "Query EvidenceReviewContext, the selected read-only comparison table. Start with EvidenceReviewContext | take 10 to inspect available scope and provenance. No joins are needed or supported by the evidence. TestEventId identifies the STREAMING package only, not the administrative SQL reference. For Kadena or test-integrated-defense-001 questions, retrieve the context row without filtering TestEventId to that administrative identity; inspect ReferenceContent, ReferenceDocumentId, ReferenceSourcePath, ReferenceLimitations and ContextLimitations alongside PackageId, TestEventId and SourcePath. Co-location is not linkage. Top-level Counts, Review, RecordedClock, FollowOnObservations, SyntheticRuleNotice, Source and Limitations are verified projections of Package; RawRecords preserves source lines and Rules contains the complete rule document. Return source values, not invented fields. For timing compute datetime_diff('second', todatetime(FollowOnObservations[0].due_utc), todatetime(RecordedClock.last_recorded_event_utc)) and report the gap explicitly. All thresholds are synthetic. Retrieve the full row when explaining evidence boundaries; the result is one small recorded fixture, not historical replay counts.",
  "displayName": "kqldb_mda_test",
  "type": "kusto",
  "userDescription": "EvidenceReviewContext provides a join-free, read-only comparison of the recorded test-streaming-findings-001 evidence package and the separate checked-in administrative SQL seed describing test-integrated-defense-001 and Kadena. It contains the full package, source-line raw records, rules, and independently identified reference document. The table's TestEventId belongs only to the streaming package. Administrative reference questions require reading the same row without filtering that field to the administrative event. The separate source IDs and limitations explicitly establish no event linkage, current closure, approval or execution authorization.",
  "metadata": null,
